IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `ea1-part4b-benefits`

-- Tests for ea1-part4b-benefits.l4 (ss 45 to 53).  Every expected value is written from
-- the text of the section (inputs/EmA1968.txt) before the function was run.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 45 Payment of retrenchment benefit`
-- Service began on 1 January 2024: two years are complete on 1 January 2026.
-- arguments are: the day service began, the day of dismissal, dismissed on the ground of redundancy or by reorganisation.
#ASSERT `s 45 the employee is entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 45 the employee is entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 45 the employee is entitled to a retrenchment benefit on dismissal` (Date 1 1 2024) (Date 31 12 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 46 Retirement benefit`
-- Service began on 1 January 2020: five years are complete on 1 January 2025.
-- arguments are: the day service began, the day service ceased, the benefit is one other than the sums payable under the CPF Act.
#ASSERT `s 46 the employee is entitled to a retirement benefit on the cessation of service` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 31 12 2024) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 46 the employee is entitled to a retirement benefit on the cessation of service` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 1 1 2025) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 46 the employee is entitled to a retirement benefit on the cessation of service` (Date 1 1 2020) (Date 31 12 2024) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 47 Priority of retirement benefits, etc.`
-- (1): arguments are: the proceeding, a collective agreement or award contains the provision, the gratuity is due and owing.
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(a) the winding up of a company under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(b) the distribution of the property of a bankrupt or of a person dying insolvent under section 352 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(c) the winding up of a VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(d) the winding up of a VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(e) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(f) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 47(1) "Where a collective agreement or an award contains a provision ... the gratuity or other sum of money which is due and owing": a "Where" not met: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(a) the winding up of a company under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1)(a) the winding up of a company under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money is included among the debts to be paid in priority` `s 47(1) some other proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the rank: after the preferential debts in (a), (c), (d), (e) and (f); (b) is silent.
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1)(a) the winding up of a company under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1)(c) the winding up of a VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1)(d) the winding up of a VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1)(e) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under the repealed section 328 of the Companies Act 1967 as applied before the operative date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1)(f) the winding up of a sub-fund of an umbrella VCC under section 203 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 as applied on the operative date` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1)(b) the distribution of the property of a bankrupt or of a person dying insolvent under section 352 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(1) the gratuity or sum of money ranks after the preferential debts` `s 47(1) some other proceeding` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): arguments are: a retirement provision, no provision for the contingency, the employer ceased or transferred, the employee ceased by reason of it, subsection (3) takes (2) away.
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 47(2) "Where a collective agreement or an award contains a provision ... on his or her retirement and no provision is made for": a "Where" not met: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); and (3): "Subsection (2) does not apply where an employer has set up a fund": no.
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the collective agreement or award is deemed to contain the provision that the employee must be paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the sum of money the employee must be paid` 5000 (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the sum of money the employee must be paid` 5000 (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(2) the sum of money the employee must be paid` 5000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3), (4)
#ASSERT `s 47(3) subsection (2) applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(3) subsection (2) applies` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(4) the sum is a payment on retirement included among the debts referred to in subsection (1)(a) or (b)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(4) the sum is a payment on retirement included among the debts referred to in subsection (1)(a) or (b)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): the definitions.
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "award" the award is one` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 47(5) "award" the award is one` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "collective agreement" the agreement is one` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 47(5) "collective agreement" the agreement is one` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "company" the body is one` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "company" the body is one` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "operative date" the date` (JUST (Date 1 1 2020)) EQUALS JUST (Date 1 1 2020)
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "operative date" the date` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "sub-fund", "umbrella VCC" and "VCC" the body is one` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "sub-fund", "umbrella VCC" and "VCC" the body is one` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 47(5) "VCC Act" the statute is the VCC Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 47(5) "VCC Act" the statute is the VCC Act` FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 48 Payment of annual wage supplement or other variable payment`
-- (1): arguments are: the day made, it provides for the payment, the parties have agreed to vary.  The date is 26 August 1988.
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the payments continue to be payable by the employer` (Date 25 8 1988) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the payments continue to be payable by the employer` (Date 25 8 1988) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- made on 26 August 1988 is not "before 26 August 1988".
-- s 48(1) "made before 26 August 1988": a contract made on that day is outside the period the text fixes (ruled 2026-11-05 (a)); and a contract that provides for no such payment leaves the "Where" unmet (b).
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the payments continue to be payable by the employer` (Date 26 8 1988) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(1) the payments continue to be payable by the employer` (Date 25 8 1988) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(2) the parties may negotiate for and agree to a variable payment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(2) the parties may negotiate for and agree to a variable payment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): arguments are: the employer paid before 26 August 1988, the day made, the supplement the provision allows, one month's wages.
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the contract of service or collective agreement may contain the provision for the annual wage supplement` FALSE (Date 1 9 1988) 2000 1500 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the contract of service or collective agreement may contain the provision for the annual wage supplement` FALSE (Date 1 9 1988) 1500 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the contract of service or collective agreement may contain the provision for the annual wage supplement` TRUE (Date 1 9 1988) 2000 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the contract of service or collective agreement may contain the provision for the annual wage supplement` FALSE (Date 25 8 1988) 2000 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- "on or after that date": made on 26 August 1988 itself is within the subsection.
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the contract of service or collective agreement may contain the provision for the annual wage supplement` FALSE (Date 26 8 1988) 2000 1500 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4): arguments are: requests or invites, the supplement requested, one month's wages.
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the person or trade union that requests or invites negotiations is guilty of an offence` TRUE 2000 1500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the person or trade union that requests or invites negotiations is guilty of an offence` TRUE 1500 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the person or trade union that requests or invites negotiations is guilty of an offence` FALSE 2000 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the employer that pays an annual wage supplement above the amount in subsection (3) is guilty of an offence` TRUE 2000 1500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the employer that pays an annual wage supplement above the amount in subsection (3) is guilty of an offence` TRUE 1500 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the employer that pays an annual wage supplement above the amount in subsection (3) is guilty of an offence` FALSE 2000 1500 EQUALS NOTHING
`a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 1000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING
`a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 2000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the penalty on conviction` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) FALSE EQUALS JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the penalty on conviction` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 48(4) the penalty on conviction` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5)
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the employer may invite the employees or a trade union to negotiate for a lower annual wage supplement or none` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 48(5) "in the event of exceptionally poor business results": not poor, no ("in the event of" read as "where": fork F-EVENT).
#ASSERT `s 48(5) the employer may invite the employees or a trade union to negotiate for a lower annual wage supplement or none` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 49 Power of Minister to make recommendations for wage adjustments`
#ASSERT `s 49 the Minister may make recommendations for wage adjustment` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 49 the Minister may make recommendations for wage adjustment` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 49 the employer and the employer's employees or a trade union may negotiate based on the recommendations` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 49 "upon the publication of the recommendations in the Gazette": not yet published, no ("upon" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 49 the employer and the employer's employees or a trade union may negotiate based on the recommendations` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 50 Interpretation for purposes of sections 48 and 49`
#ASSERT `s 50(1) either party may refer the matter to the Industrial Arbitration Court for arbitration` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 50(1) "Where a notice is served ... and no agreement is reached": a "Where" not met, no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 50(1) either party may refer the matter to the Industrial Arbitration Court for arbitration` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 50(1) either party may refer the matter to the Industrial Arbitration Court for arbitration` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments are: a single annual payment to employees, supplemental to the total annual wages.
#ASSERT `s 50(2) "annual wage supplement" the payment is one` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(2) "annual wage supplement" the payment is one` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(2) "annual wage supplement" the payment is one` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 50(2) "variable payment" the payment is one` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 50(2) "variable payment" the payment is one` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(2) "variable payment" the payment is one` FALSE FALSE)
-- "wages": basic wages, and not a commission, overtime allowance or other allowance.
#ASSERT `s 50(2) "wages" the payment is wages` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(2) "wages" the payment is wages` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 50(2) "wages" the payment is wages` FALSE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 52 Power to suspend application of this Part`
#ASSERT `s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 52 "when the public interest so requires it": the public interest does not require it, no ("when" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 53 Offence`
#ASSERT `s 53 the employer is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 53 the employer is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 53 the employer is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a first offence: a fine up to $5,000 and no imprisonment; a second or later: up to $10,000 or 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 53 the penalty on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING)
#ASSERT `s 53 the penalty on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 10000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)
#ASSERT `s 53 the penalty on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Added with the rulings of 2026-11-05: s 48(3) as a "Where" of its own, and the s 52 cases that remain not covered.
-- The cap binds an employer that paid no annual wage supplement before 26 August 1988, for a contract made on or after that date.
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the cap of one month's wages on the annual wage supplement applies` FALSE (Date 26 8 1988) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the cap of one month's wages on the annual wage supplement applies` FALSE (Date 25 8 1988) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 48(3) the cap of one month's wages on the annual wage supplement applies` TRUE (Date 1 3 1990) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 52: the public interest requires it, but no notification has been made: the power is not exercised, not covered.
#ASSERT `s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 52: a notification suspends the provision for a class, the public interest requires it, the employee is in the class.
#ASSERT `s 52 the provision of Part 4 is suspended for the employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
